## Test that drbdmeta writes only the one layout that an indexed meta data
## device can hold: a 32 KB activity log and 4096 bytes per bitmap bit.
##
## Bug guarded against: the slot an index names is 128 MB with fixed offsets,
## and DRBD refuses to attach anything else there ("meta data offsets don't
## make sense").  drbdmeta still laid out activity log striping as asked, and
## max_usable_sectors() ran into its own assertion for any other bitmap
## granularity: "ASSERT((cfg->md.bm_bytes_per_bit == 4096)) failed", abort.
##
## Test layout: a 192 MB image as the meta data device, index 0.  The default
## layout is written, everything else refused, for v08 and v09 alike.
## Flexible meta data, which sizes itself after the device, keeps taking both.

$ tmpdir=$(mktemp -d) && img=$(mktemp --suffix=.img)
$ truncate -s 201326592 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" 0 create-md --effective-size 1000000 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" 0 dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .md_size_sect, .al_offset, .bm_offset, .al_stripes, .al_stripe_size_4k]'
[4096,262144,8,72,1,8]
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" 0 create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 1000000 1 2>&1 >/dev/null | tail -5; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
Meta data at index 0 asks for an activity log of 32 KB and
8192 bytes per bitmap bit.  The fixed size slot of an indexed
meta data device takes only 32 KB and 4096 bytes per bitmap
bit; DRBD would refuse to attach anything else.
Use a meta data device of its own instead of an index.
10
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" 0 create-md --al-stripes 4 --al-stripe-size 32 --effective-size 1000000 1 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^Meta data at index'; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
Meta data at index 0 asks for an activity log of 128 KB and
10
$ drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" 0 dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .bm_offset, .al_stripes, .["#meta"].valid]'
[4096,72,1,"VALID_MD_FOUND"]
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 201326592 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" 0 create-md --al-stripes 4 --al-stripe-size 32 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^Meta data at index'; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
Meta data at index 0 asks for an activity log of 128 KB and
10
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 201326592 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-external create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --al-stripes 4 --al-stripe-size 32 --effective-size 1000000 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-external dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .al_stripes, .al_stripe_size_4k]'
[8192,4,8]
$ rm -rf "$tmpdir" "$img"
